From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Dodaskot <pessdres@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 10 Nov 2026 06:17:13 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 5/5] drm/mediatek: draw the A22x boot splash

Draw a logo straight into the fbdev buffer as soon as it exists, which
is before /init runs. Plymouth does the same from userspace but needs a
much larger initramfs and starts later.

CONFIG_DRM_MEDIATEK_BOOT_SPLASH draws a progress bar for the recovery:
its interface reads boot_splash_percent, writes boot_splash_stop and
carries the bar on to 100%. With CONFIG_DRM_MEDIATEK_BOOT_SPLASH_SWEEP,
for the system kernel, a light runs to and fro under the logo instead,
until a compositor or greeter becomes DRM master (a new master_set
callback of the driver) or SPLASH_SWEEP_LIMIT_MS have passed.
boot_splash_show draws the splash again, for shutdown.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 drivers/gpu/drm/mediatek/Kconfig              |    15 +
 drivers/gpu/drm/mediatek/Makefile             |     2 +
 drivers/gpu/drm/mediatek/mtk_boot_splash.c    |   225 +
 drivers/gpu/drm/mediatek/mtk_boot_splash.h    |    15 +
 .../gpu/drm/mediatek/mtk_boot_splash_logo.h   | 38569 ++++++++++++++++
 drivers/gpu/drm/mediatek/mtk_drm_drv.c        |     9 +
 6 files changed, 38835 insertions(+)
 create mode 100644 drivers/gpu/drm/mediatek/mtk_boot_splash.c
 create mode 100644 drivers/gpu/drm/mediatek/mtk_boot_splash.h
